# Master Workshop Exercise Prompt

Distributed to attendees during Module 3. Paste this into the primary prompt bar at [lovable.dev](https://lovable.dev) and click **Create Project**.

```
Act as a Lead Product Designer and Full-Stack Developer.

Build a modern, high-converting web application for a local sustainable
retail brand called "EcoShift Marketplace".

Design Guidelines:
- Color Palette: Clean earth tones (forest green accents, soft off-white
  background, dark slate text).
- Responsive layout optimized for mobile and desktop screens.

Key Page Components:
1. Hero Section: Catchy headline ("Sustainable Shopping Made Simple"),
   short subtitle, and a primary CTA button ("Explore Catalog").
2. Interactive Product Catalog: Display 4 sample products (Reusable
   Bamboo Tote, Solar Power Bank, Compostable Phone Case, Organic
   Cotton Shirt) with placeholder images, prices, and category tags.
3. Filtering & Search: Allow users to filter products by Category and
   search by product title in real-time.
4. Interactive Shopping Cart: A side-drawer shopping cart where users
   can add items, increment/decrement quantities, and view a
   real-time calculated total price.
5. Impact Calculator Widget: A quick interactive slider where users
   select their estimated monthly purchases (1 to 20 items) to
   display real-time calculated savings of plastic waste (e.g., "You
   saved X kg of plastic waste this year!").
```

## Follow-up Prompts Used Live

**Visual edit (click the Hero CTA button, then type):**
```
Make this button forest green with rounded-full corners, a subtle
hover scale effect, and shadow-md.
```

**Feature expansion (chat panel):**
```
Add a category filter dropdown above the product grid with options:
All, Home, Electronics, Apparel. Wire this directly to product state.
```

**Backend / database (Module 4):**
```
Store customer orders in a database table called orders. Include
columns for customer_email, total_amount, order_items (JSON), and
created_at. Ensure Row Level Security (RLS) is enabled so users only
see their own data.
```
